# requires: macos
# Session restore brings a terminal pane back DORMANT — its tab, its
# title and `[exited]`, waiting for a key — never a running shell.
# Neovim's `:mksession` does not restore `:terminal` buffers as live
# processes either, and a shell that starts itself in a workspace runs
# that workspace's rc files (and whatever the last one was in the middle
# of) without being asked.
write notes.txt "alpha\n"
open notes.txt
# The TERMINAL mode chip is the vim profile's reading of a focused pty
# pane (`statusline.modeOf`), and `<leader>h` is where the shell lives.
command editor.use_vim
command term.shell_bottom
wait 2000
expect screen contains "TERMINAL"
expect screen lacks "any key restarts"

# The pane IS saved — losing the tab would be its own bug.
command session.save
expect file .mnml/session.zon contains "pty"

command session.restore
wait 500
expect screen contains "session restored"
expect screen contains "[exited] — any key restarts"

# And a key on it starts the child the restore did not.
key enter
wait 1500
expect screen lacks "any key restarts"
